// Title: Renamed ProcDump Execution
// ID: 4a0b2c7e-7cb2-495d-8b63-5f268e7bfd67
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-11-18
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036.003
// Description: Detects the execution of a renamed ProcDump executable.
// This often done by attackers or malware in order to evade defensive mechanisms.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((OriginalFileName = "procdump") OR (((src.process.cmdline containsCIS " -ma " OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " -mp ")) AND (src.process.cmdline containsCIS " /accepteula"))) AND NOT (((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\procdump.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\procdump64.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\procdump64a.exe"))))
